+**CPU KV offload in the deployment.** Offload is off by default. Set `KV_OFFLOAD_GIB` (GiB, e.g. 12
+on both `vllm-0`/`vllm-1`) to enable it; both instances share the host `/dev/shm`, so the two tiers
+must sum to <= ~28 G.
+
+**Shared fs (disk) tier — the recommended mode.** One command sets up the whole host side:
+
+```bash
+sudo ./ops/setup-kv-offload.sh              # 12 GiB RAM/instance, 100 GiB disk cap
+# sudo ./ops/setup-kv-offload.sh --volume-gib 500   # reserve a fixed 500 GiB volume instead
+# sudo ./ops/setup-kv-offload.sh --uninstall        # reverse it
+# ./ops/setup-kv-offload.sh --dry-run               # preview, change nothing
+```
+
+It prepares the disk-tier directory (or a reserved fixed-size volume), installs and starts the
+**mandatory reaper** (the tier never deletes on its own) with the GiB cap, and prints the two
+Coolify variables to set on **both** services:
+
+```
+KV_OFFLOAD_GIB=12
+KV_OFFLOAD_DISK_HOST_DIR=/var/lib/radiance-kvcache
+```
+
+The compose mounts that host dir at `/kvcache` in both instances and `KV_OFFLOAD_DISK_DIR`
+defaults to `/kvcache/blocks`, so a prefix cached by one replica is loadable by the other and
+survives restarts. With the disk holding the overflow, **no per-request head cap is needed**.
+
+A prefix cache is per instance, so send a stable `x-session-id` header to keep a conversation on one
+replica (HAProxy sticks on it; clients without the header keep `leastconn`). Full analysis, tier
+comparison, disk sizing, and runbook: `PERFORMANCE.md` -> "Productionizing the CPU/disk KV offload".
+
